ntestable** when a careful, reasonable colleague could still argue that it meets the request (for\n  example, \"the Pricing sheet file\" when the record is \"Pricing sheet 2025.xlsx\"). Say so for that record; it is\n  not the same as failing nothing.\n\nBe precise. Judge each condition on its own; do not let one record's overall fit sway you. When a condition turns on\na time, compute it in the stated time zone. When it turns on a person, match the exact person.\n\n\n---\n\nA user of Slack gave an assistant this request:\n\n> In my DM with Diego Alvarez, add a raised-hands reaction to the message he posted about the Meridian invoice deadline.\n\nThe person making the request is the workspace's assistant bot (U01AGENBOT9), acting for the team.\n\nStep 1: list the conditions a record must meet for this request to refer to it, and every phrase that could reasonably be read in more than one way.","run_stream":{"id":"f156cae0-378f-4bf4-aef1-8411d47128cc","kind":"run"}}}
